cfMesh (mesh generation library based on OpenFOAM)
    Source: https://develop.openfoam.com/Community/integration-cfmesh
    Upstream: Creative Fields, Ltd. — Franjo Juretic
    Copyright: (C) 2014-2017 Creative Fields, Ltd. + later contributors
    License: GNU General Public License, version 3 or later (GPL-3.0-or-later)
    License file: third_party/cfmesh/LICENSE.GPL3
    Per-file headers retained: every .H/.C file in third_party/cfmesh/ contains
    the original GPL-3 notice.

    Vendored as the GPL-3 mesh-generation backend for AutoTessell. AutoTessell
    is licensed GPL-3.0-or-later (project-wide) to remain compatible with this
    vendored sub-tree (see project root LICENSE). No modifications to cfMesh
    sources; only build glue (CMakeLists.txt for wmake → cmake) + pybind11
    binding glue (auto_tessell_core/cfmesh_bind.cpp).

    cfMesh internally requires a small subset of OpenFOAM core headers
    (dictionary, IOobject, polyMesh I/O, Time). These are provided either:
      (a) via a minimal in-tree stub at third_party/cfmesh/openfoam_min/, or
      (b) by linking against a system OpenFOAM installation if detected.

    Tools provided after build:
      cartesianMesh — hex-dominant cartesian mesher (snappyHexMesh competitor)
      tetMesh       — Delaunay-based tet mesher (used as tet fallback only;
                       primary tet path remains vendored fTetWild)
      pMesh         — polyhedral mesher (default backend for mesh_type=poly)
